t.card(t.wo['performance_tasks'][1],'02 03 04 05',data+' Describe three economies/diseconomies, each with its distinguishing case detail (6). Explain how these mechanisms affect unit costs at the two scales (7). Discuss whether further expansion is justified by cost and firm-size conditions (7).','Technical specialisation saves N$2, purchasing N$1 and coordination adds N$1 initially. The savings total N$3; first expansion has a net N$2 average-cost fall, but at further scale N$4 coordination exceeds them and unit cost rises N$1. Further expansion is poorly supported: the unit-cost balance worsens, the market is narrow and finance is not secured. Potential gains remain, but changed organisation, sustained buyers and affordable funds would be needed to strengthen the case.',['Data description (6): technical economy (1), N$2 specialisation detail (1); purchasing economy (1), N$1 detail (1); coordination diseconomy (1), N$1 delay detail (1). Mechanism/explanation (7): specialisation improves resource use (1), purchasing lowers input cost (1), total saving N$3 (1); coordination consumes resources (1), first net fall N$2 (1), later coordination N$4 (1), later net rise N$1 (1). Both sides/judgement (7): potential scale savings (1), organisation might improve (1); net cost worsens (1), narrow market (1), unsecured capital condition (1); judgement further growth not justified now (1), tied to sales/funding/coordination constraints (1). Marks allocation 6+7+7=20.'],[data])
